00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:18.647
- The first Passover was when
the Jews were still in Egypt.

00:07:19.765 --> 00:07:23.758
They were shut up in their
homes, they were anxious,

00:07:23.758 --> 00:07:25.999
they were scared, they
didn't know the future

00:07:25.999 --> 00:07:29.230
and there was blood on the doorposts.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:34.230
This Passover is in a way
reminiscent of the very first,

00:07:34.644 --> 00:07:38.210
different from any that we have ever

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:40.543
celebrated in our lifetimes.

00:07:41.728 --> 00:07:45.232
But remember what happened later,

00:07:45.232 --> 00:07:48.956
that Passover gave way to deliverance

00:07:48.956 --> 00:07:51.519
and that even though it began in darkness,

00:07:51.519 --> 00:07:53.029
it ended in light.

00:07:53.029 --> 00:07:55.946
(soft piano music)

00:07:57.397 --> 00:08:02.261
- I and a bunch of other people
got together and we ended up

00:08:02.261 --> 00:08:04.706
doing this thing called a Memory Feast.

00:08:04.706 --> 00:08:06.921
So what we did was we
brought all of this food

00:08:06.921 --> 00:08:09.435
and all of this drink, but
each thing that we brought

00:08:09.435 --> 00:08:12.007
had to be connected to a specific memory.

00:08:12.007 --> 00:08:13.735
And it was just a great experience

00:08:13.735 --> 00:08:15.382
to not only be able to share that,

00:08:15.382 --> 00:08:17.927
but to feel more connected with them

00:08:17.927 --> 00:08:20.720
because they also shared stories,

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:23.681
sweet stories of their own backgrounds

00:08:23.681 --> 00:08:24.809
and their own childhoods.

00:08:24.809 --> 00:08:26.804
- My younger son reenacts the story

00:08:26.804 --> 00:08:30.329
