00:50:37.993 --> 00:50:41.326
and all Jewish holidays
into three simple sentences.

00:50:41.326 --> 00:50:45.484
They tried to kill us,
we survived, let's eat.

00:50:45.484 --> 00:50:47.753
During this Passover with the coronavirus,

00:50:47.753 --> 00:50:50.053
unfortunately, those words are no joke,

00:50:50.053 --> 00:50:52.241
they are all reality.

00:50:52.241 --> 00:50:54.998
But I know how many of us feel isolated

00:50:54.998 --> 00:50:58.999
and uncertain about the
future, frightened right now.

00:50:58.999 --> 00:51:02.190
But we Jews know the
power of perseverance,

00:51:02.190 --> 00:51:04.732
that's how we've survived
over the centuries.

00:51:04.732 --> 00:51:07.489
Sticking together, giving
each other strength

00:51:07.489 --> 00:51:11.169
and moral support and
overcoming the worst,

00:51:11.169 --> 00:51:14.868
the worst of afflictions and persecutions.

00:51:14.868 --> 00:51:17.271
So, together we will overcome this plague

00:51:17.271 --> 00:51:22.101
like everyone before it, so
that we can be happy, healthy,

00:51:22.101 --> 00:51:26.740
free once again, and we
can have our next Seder,

00:51:26.740 --> 00:51:29.510
maybe not in Jerusalem, but all together

00:51:29.510 --> 00:51:31.517
with our family and friends.

00:51:31.517 --> 00:51:34.766
To all of you, a decent Pesach.

00:51:34.766 --> 00:51:38.541
- Yeah, it's Passover, yes!

00:51:38.541 --> 00:51:40.520
- Passover is a journey,

00:51:40.520 --> 00:51:43.227
a journey within where we pull
back the layers of our soul,

00:51:43.227 --> 00:51:44.467
we look inwards.

00:51:44.467 --> 00:51:49.467
- What you realize from this
communal holiday is that--

00:51:49.485 --> 00:51:50.866
- We all are alike.

00:51:50.866 --> 00:51:52.943
- It doesn't matter where
you're from or what you do,

00:51:52.943 --> 00:51:54.068
how much you know.

00:51:54.068 --> 00:51:57.532
- Rituals may change, the
language and methods of observance

00:51:57.532 --> 00:51:58.525
may change but--

00:51:58.525 --> 00:52:01.003
- The beliefs and what we
share and what we hold dear

00:52:01.003 --> 00:52:05.039
to one another, our families,
our annoying relatives

00:52:05.039 --> 00:52:08.265
who wanna constantly question
who is in our love life

00:52:08.265 --> 00:52:09.285
and who isn't.

00:52:09.285 --> 00:52:11.013
- We're all the same, we're all connected.

00:52:11.013 --> 00:52:12.509
Each and every one of us is holy,

00:52:12.509 --> 00:52:14.007
is connected to our creator.

00:52:14.007 --> 00:52:15.778
- But ultimately, Jews are just people

00:52:15.778 --> 00:52:19.243
who want to get together,
just sit in solid silence,

00:52:19.243 --> 00:52:21.996
just waiting for someone to finish talking

00:52:21.996 --> 00:52:24.505
so they can get some food in their faces.

00:52:24.505 --> 00:52:25.752
- And through that together,

00:52:25.752 --> 00:52:28.267
experiencing that unity as individuals

00:52:28.267 --> 00:52:30.985
or experiences as a people and as a world

00:52:30.985 --> 00:52:32.253
and bring goodness for
each and every one of us

00:52:32.253 --> 00:52:33.252
in our lives.

00:52:33.252 --> 00:52:35.205
- Happy Passover.

00:52:35.205 --> 00:52:38.356
(gentle piano music)

00:52:38.356 --> 00:52:42.216
- I'm taken back to a story
that is thousands of years old.

00:52:42.216 --> 00:52:44.743
This story that we told tonight,

00:52:44.743 --> 00:52:48.256
a story that's held a grip
on the human imagination

00:52:48.256 --> 00:52:50.492
for thousands of years.

00:52:50.492 --> 00:52:52.761
Precisely because it was never just about

00:52:52.761 --> 00:52:57.000
what happened then, but
has also always been about

00:52:57.000 --> 00:52:58.613
what's happening now.

00:52:58.613 --> 00:53:00.768
It's never been just about
what happened to them,

00:53:00.768 --> 00:53:04.708
but it's always been about
what's also happening to us.

00:53:04.708 --> 00:53:07.121
This is a story of an Israelite people

00:53:07.121 --> 00:53:10.675
who were degraded and
oppressed and enslaved,

00:53:10.675 --> 00:53:14.233
and then somehow through
the series of miracles,

00:53:14.233 --> 00:53:17.146
both divine and human, were able to begin

00:53:17.146 --> 00:53:20.235
to walk on that long
journey toward freedom.

00:53:20.235 --> 00:53:22.258
This is a story in the
language of our Rabbis,

00:53:22.258 --> 00:53:23.765
(speaks in foreign language)

00:53:23.765 --> 00:53:26.445
of a trajectory that takes
us from darkness to light.

00:53:26.445 --> 00:53:28.964
(speaks in foreign language)

00:53:28.964 --> 00:53:32.999
From anguish to joy, from
grief to celebration,

00:53:32.999 --> 00:53:36.242
from narrowness to great expansiveness,

00:53:36.242 --> 00:53:38.575
from degradation to dignity.

00:53:39.757 --> 00:53:41.943
And our rabbis understood
that that was a message

00:53:41.943 --> 00:53:43.828
that we needed to hear not only once,

00:53:43.828 --> 00:53:47.140
but needed to be built into our DNA

00:53:47.140 --> 00:53:50.669
so that we would have the
muscle memory for hope

00:53:50.669 --> 00:53:54.455
exactly in moments like the
ones we're living in right now,

00:53:54.455 --> 00:53:55.604
when we need hope the most.

00:53:55.604 --> 00:53:58.153
In fact, this story is
the closest thing we have

00:53:58.153 --> 00:54:01.065
to the genetic transmission of hope

00:54:01.065 --> 00:54:05.255
because it tells us that even
though things are painful

00:54:05.255 --> 00:54:08.982
and hard, and we are incredibly
vulnerable right now,

00:54:08.982 --> 00:54:12.894
that we will survive this,
that our story doesn't end here

00:54:12.894 --> 00:54:15.998
and that we, like those who
came before us, will one day

00:54:15.998 --> 00:54:19.796
come to the other side of
this plague of darkness.

00:54:19.796 --> 00:54:24.703
And when we do, we will grieve
and then we will rebuild.

00:54:24.703 --> 00:54:26.968
And I pray on this night

00:54:26.968 --> 00:54:30.213
that we will do what the
Israelites did so many years ago.

00:54:30.213 --> 00:54:33.253
They rebuilt a society
that was the counter Egypt,

00:54:33.253 --> 00:54:35.995
that was the antithesis
of what they'd experienced

00:54:35.995 --> 00:54:37.465
in their suffering in Egypt.

00:54:37.465 --> 00:54:40.502
And we will build a
society that is counter

00:54:40.502 --> 00:54:42.199
to the injustices and oppressions

00:54:42.199 --> 00:54:45.441
and indignities of this
world that we have lived in.

00:54:45.441 --> 00:54:48.274
And instead we'll build
a world rooted in justice

00:54:48.274 --> 00:54:50.967
and equity and equality
and dignity for all people

00:54:50.967 --> 00:54:53.271
and most of all, in love.

00:54:53.271 --> 00:54:57.354
And that will be a beautiful
world for all of us.

